silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_01_kleisli_category_overview_concrete_anchor_5 silm:hasExample "In 'KleisliOverviewAnchorProfile', the bare-symbol→anchor table grounds the abstract symbols in the Tartu-Animal-Clinic / Mittens-2026-05-18 domain story. For example, Profile is the terminal node of the four-step Kleisli pipeline, produced by profile^Kl. For Mittens it instantiates to the pair (Y^in_Mittens, Y^out_Mittens): the incoming hom-functor Hom(-, Mittens) and outgoing hom-functor Hom(Mittens, -). The profile encodes every typed arrow into Mittens (record, identifier, quality, measurement, role, process, validation, trace, classification, taxonomy legs) and every typed arrow out of Mittens (classification target DomesticCat, derived facts, audit traces). Downstream papers inherit Mittens through this profile; the Yoneda lemma guarantees this fixes Mittens up to isomorphism.." .
